# Better Auth

## Contents

- [Install](#install)
- [Server setup](#server-setup)
- [Browser client](#browser-client)
- [Checkout, portal and billing history](#checkout-portal-and-billing-history)
- [Usage events](#usage-events)
- [Webhooks and routes](#webhooks-and-routes)
- [Common mistakes](#common-mistakes)

`@dodopayments/better-auth` creates a Dodo customer for each Better Auth user and adds authenticated checkout, customer portal, billing history, usage and webhook endpoints. Use it instead of a framework adapter when the app uses Better Auth.

## Install

```bash
npm install @dodopayments/better-auth dodopayments better-auth zod
```

Needs Better Auth 1.4 or a later 1.x.

## Server setup

Each endpoint exists only if its feature is in `use`.

```typescript
import { betterAuth } from "better-auth";
import DodoPayments from "dodopayments";
import { checkout, dodopayments, portal, usage, webhooks } from "@dodopayments/better-auth";

const dodoPayments = new DodoPayments({
  bearerToken: process.env.DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY,
  environment: process.env.DODO_PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT === "live_mode" ? "live_mode" : "test_mode",
});

export const auth = betterAuth({
  database: {
    // your database config
  },
  plugins: [
    dodopayments({
      client: dodoPayments,
      createCustomerOnSignUp: true,
      getCustomerParams: (user) => ({ metadata: { better_auth_user_id: user.id } }),
      use: [
        checkout({
          products: [{ productId: "pdt_pro_monthly", slug: "pro" }],
          successUrl: "https://example.com/billing/success",
          authenticatedUsersOnly: true,
        }),
        portal(),
        usage(),
        webhooks({
          webhookKey: process.env.DODO_PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_KEY,
          onPayload: async (payload) => {
            console.log("Verified Dodo webhook:", payload.type);
          },
        }),
      ],
    }),
  ],
});
```

- `products` maps your slug to a Dodo product ID, so the browser never picks a product ID.
- The plugin adds `dodoCustomerId` to the `user` table. Update the schema with `npx auth generate` (then apply it) or `npx auth migrate`.
- `getCustomerParams` sees only Better Auth's base user fields unless you declare `user.additionalFields`.

## Browser client

```typescript
import { createAuthClient } from "better-auth/react";
import { dodopaymentsClient } from "@dodopayments/better-auth/client";

export const authClient = createAuthClient({ plugins: [dodopaymentsClient()] });
```

The client sends the session cookie itself; do not pass `headers`.

## Checkout, portal and billing history

```typescript
const { data: session, error } = await authClient.dodopayments.checkoutSession({
  slug: "pro",
  referenceId: "order_123", // optional
});
if (!error && session) window.location.href = session.url;

const { data: portalSession } = await authClient.dodopayments.customer.portal();
if (portalSession?.redirect) window.location.href = portalSession.url;

const { data: subscriptions } = await authClient.dodopayments.customer.subscriptions.list({
  query: { page: 1, limit: 10, status: "active" },
});
const { data: payments } = await authClient.dodopayments.customer.payments.list({
  query: { page: 1, limit: 10, status: "succeeded" },
});
console.log(subscriptions?.items, payments?.items);
```

The portal needs a signed-in user with a verified email.

## Usage events

```typescript
const { data, error } = await authClient.dodopayments.usage.ingest({
  event_id: "api-call:req_123", // reuse on retry
  event_name: "api.call",
  metadata: { endpoint: "/v1/users" },
  timestamp: new Date(),
});
if (error) console.error(error);
else console.log(data?.ingested_count);
```

The plugin sets `customer_id` from the session. `usage.ingest` and `usage.meters.list` need a verified email. For usage that the server records, ingest from the server instead ([usage-billing.md](usage-billing.md)).

## Webhooks and routes

`webhooks({ webhookKey, onPayload })` reads the raw body, verifies the signature and calls `onPayload`. Register this URL in the Dodo dashboard (default base path `/api/auth`):

```text
https://example.com/api/auth/dodopayments/webhooks
```

Routes under the Better Auth base path: `POST /dodopayments/checkout`, `POST /dodopayments/checkout-session`, `GET /dodopayments/customer/portal`, `GET /dodopayments/customer/subscriptions/list`, `GET /dodopayments/customer/payments/list`, `POST /dodopayments/usage/ingest`, `GET /dodopayments/usage/meters/list`, `POST /dodopayments/webhooks`.

## Common mistakes

- Leaving a feature out of `use`; its route returns 404.
- Calling `client.customers.create` as well as `createCustomerOnSignUp`; it duplicates customers.
- Adding a second webhook route or calling `auth.api.dodopayments.verifyWebhook()`, which does not exist.
- Granting access from browser state instead of the verified webhook.

# BillingSDK

## Contents

- [What it is](#what-it-is)
- [Install components](#install-components)
- [Component inventory](#component-inventory)
- [Pricing page](#pricing-page)
- [Manage billing button](#manage-billing-button)
- [Usage and credit display](#usage-and-credit-display)
- [Theming](#theming)
- [Common mistakes](#common-mistakes)

## What it is

BillingSDK (`github.com/dodopayments/billingsdk`) is an open-source set of React components for pricing and billing UI, built on Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui. Components are copied into your repo as source, like shadcn/ui; there is no runtime npm package to install.

- Components only render data and fire callbacks. Every Dodo call happens in your server routes.
- The installed file under `components/billingsdk/` is the prop contract for your version. Read its exported props type before wiring callbacks.
- `registry.json` in the repo lists what is installable.
- React and Next.js only. For other front ends, use a framework adapter ([framework-adapters.md](framework-adapters.md)) and your own UI.

## Install components

```bash
npx @billingsdk/cli init                         # scaffold routes, hooks, lib/dodopayments.ts and env vars
npx @billingsdk/cli add pricing-table-one        # add one component
npx shadcn@latest add @billingsdk/pricing-table-one   # same, through the shadcn registry
```

The server client lives in one module that only route handlers and server components import:

```typescript
// lib/dodopayments.ts
import DodoPayments from 'dodopayments';

export const dodo = new DodoPayments({
  bearerToken: process.env.DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY,
  environment: process.env.DODO_PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT === 'live_mode' ? 'live_mode' : 'test_mode',
});
```

## Component inventory

| Group | Components |
|---|---|
| Pricing | `pricing-table-one` to `pricing-table-eight` |
| Subscription | `subscription-management`, `usage-based-pricing`, `invoice-history`, `update-plan-card`, `update-plan-dialog`, `proration-preview`, `cancel-subscription-card`, `cancel-subscription-dialog` |
| Usage and billing | `usage-meter-linear`, `usage-meter-circle`, `usage-table`, `detailed-usage-table`, `billing-screen`, `billing-settings`, `billing-settings-2`, `upcoming-charges` |
| Payments | `payment-details`, `payment-details-two`, `payment-method-selector`, `payment-card`, `payment-failure` |
| Promotion and trials | `banner`, `limited-offer-dialog`, `trial-expiry-card` |

## Pricing page

`add pricing-table-one` generates `lib/billingsdk-config.ts` with a `Plan` type and a sample `plans` array. Edit that array. Prices there are display strings only; Dodo charges the product's price, so keep the two in sync. `onPlanSelect` receives the plan `id`, which the server maps to a product ID.

```tsx
// components/pricing-plans.tsx
'use client';

import { PricingTableOne } from '@/components/billingsdk/pricing-table-one';
import { plans } from '@/lib/billingsdk-config';

export function PricingPlans() {
  async function handlePlanSelect(planId: string) {
    const response = await fetch('/api/checkout', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ planId }),
    });
    if (!response.ok) return;
    const { checkoutUrl } = (await response.json()) as { checkoutUrl: string };
    window.location.href = checkoutUrl;
  }

  return (
    <PricingTableOne
      plans={plans}
      title="Choose your plan"
      description="Select the plan that works best for you"
      onPlanSelect={handlePlanSelect}
      theme="classic"
      size="medium"
    />
  );
}
```

The `/api/checkout` route is the Next.js route in [checkout.md](checkout.md). Its `PRODUCT_IDS` keys must equal the plan `id`s. To sell yearly plans too, create yearly products, send the billing period with the plan ID, and key the map by both.

## Manage billing button

Pair `subscription-management` (or a plain button) with the portal route in [customers.md](customers.md):

```tsx
'use client';

export function ManageBillingButton() {
  async function openPortal() {
    const response = await fetch('/api/portal', { method: 'POST' });
    if (!response.ok) return;
    const { url } = (await response.json()) as { url: string };
    window.location.href = url;
  }
  return <button type="button" onClick={openPortal}>Manage billing</button>;
}
```

Load the subscription in the server component that renders the page (`await dodo.subscriptions.retrieve(id)`) and pass plain data down.

## Usage and credit display

Read numbers on the server and pass them to `usage-meter-linear` or a related block:

```typescript
// app/api/usage/credits/route.ts
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { dodo } from '@/lib/dodopayments';
import { getCurrentUser } from '@/lib/auth';

export async function GET() {
  const user = await getCurrentUser();
  const creditEntitlementId = process.env.DODO_CREDIT_ENTITLEMENT_ID;
  if (!user?.dodoCustomerId || !creditEntitlementId) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'No billing account' }, { status: 400 });
  }
  const balance = await dodo.creditEntitlements.balances.retrieve(user.dodoCustomerId, {
    credit_entitlement_id: creditEntitlementId,
  });
  return NextResponse.json({ balance: balance.balance, overage: balance.overage });
}
```

The displayed balance lags metering by about a minute. Show it; do not gate requests on it ([credits.md](credits.md)).

## Theming

Override the shadcn CSS variables in `globals.css` for colours, use component props such as `theme` and `size`, or edit the copied source for structural changes. The hosted checkout page is themed separately through `customization` on the checkout session.

## Common mistakes

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY`. Every Dodo key is secret and must stay on the server.
- `npm install billingsdk`. The root package is private; use `@billingsdk/cli` or the shadcn registry.
- Guessing prop names instead of reading the installed component file.
- Accepting a raw `product_id` from the pricing table. Map plan IDs on the server.
- Rendering "active" from React state or `return_url` instead of the webhook-backed record in your database.

# Checkout

## Contents

- [Default: hosted checkout session](#default-hosted-checkout-session)
- [Next.js route and button](#nextjs-route-and-button)
- [Checkout session options](#checkout-session-options)
- [Response and return URL](#response-and-return-url)
- [Overlay and inline checkout](#overlay-and-inline-checkout)
- [Static payment links](#static-payment-links)
- [Retrieve and preview](#retrieve-and-preview)
- [Common mistakes](#common-mistakes)

## Default: hosted checkout session

Create a checkout session on the server with `client.checkoutSessions.create(...)` and redirect to `checkout_url`. This covers one-time products, subscriptions, trials, add-ons and discount codes. Grant access from the verified webhook ([webhooks.md](webhooks.md)), not from the redirect.

Exceptions: overlay or inline checkout when the payment form must stay on your page, and static payment links when there is no server at all.

## Next.js route and button

The browser sends a plan slug. The server authenticates the user, maps the slug to an allowlisted product ID, and returns only the URL.

```typescript
// app/api/checkout/route.ts
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import DodoPayments from 'dodopayments';
import { getCurrentUser } from '@/lib/auth';

const client = new DodoPayments({
  bearerToken: process.env.DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY,
  environment: process.env.DODO_PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT === 'live_mode' ? 'live_mode' : 'test_mode',
});

const PRODUCT_IDS: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {
  starter: 'pdt_starter_monthly',
  pro: 'pdt_pro_monthly',
};

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const user = await getCurrentUser();
  if (!user) return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Not authenticated' }, { status: 401 });

  const body = (await request.json().catch(() => null)) as { planId?: unknown } | null;
  const planId = body?.planId;
  if (typeof planId !== 'string' || !Object.hasOwn(PRODUCT_IDS, planId)) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Unknown plan' }, { status: 400 });
  }

  const session = await client.checkoutSessions.create({
    product_cart: [{ product_id: PRODUCT_IDS[planId], quantity: 1 }],
    customer: user.dodoCustomerId ? { customer_id: user.dodoCustomerId } : { email: user.email, name: user.name },
    metadata: { app_user_id: user.id },
    return_url: `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL}/checkout/success`,
  });
  return NextResponse.json({ checkoutUrl: session.checkout_url });
}
```

```tsx
// components/checkout-button.tsx
'use client';

export function CheckoutButton({ planId }: { planId: 'starter' | 'pro' }) {
  async function startCheckout() {
    const response = await fetch('/api/checkout', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ planId }),
    });
    if (!response.ok) return;
    const { checkoutUrl } = (await response.json()) as { checkoutUrl: string };
    window.location.href = checkoutUrl;
  }
  return <button onClick={startCheckout}>Buy</button>;
}
```

Express and FastAPI follow the same shape. The Express webhook route is in [webhooks.md](webhooks.md).

## Checkout session options

Add only the fields the task needs:

```typescript
const session = await client.checkoutSessions.create({
  product_cart: [
    { product_id: 'pdt_pro_monthly', quantity: 1, addons: [{ addon_id: 'adn_extra_seats', quantity: 3 }] },
  ],
  customer: { email: 'customer@example.com', name: 'Jane Doe' }, // or { customer_id: 'cus_...' }
  billing_address: { country: 'US', street: '1 Main St', city: 'San Francisco', state: 'CA', zipcode: '94105' },
  billing_currency: 'EUR', // needs Adaptive Currency, see localized-pricing.md
  tax_id: 'DE123456789',
  customer_business_name: 'Acme GmbH',
  discount_codes: ['WELCOME10'], // up to 20, applied in order
  subscription_data: { trial_period_days: 14 },
  custom_fields: [
    { key: 'company_size', label: 'Company size', field_type: 'dropdown', options: ['1-10', '11-50', '51+'], required: true },
  ],
  metadata: { app_user_id: 'user_123' },
  feature_flags: { allow_discount_code: true, allow_tax_id: true, allow_phone_number_collection: true },
  customization: { theme: 'dark', show_order_details: true, theme_config: { pay_button_text: 'Subscribe' } },
  return_url: 'https://example.com/checkout/success',
});
```

- A checkout session is single-use and expires after 24 hours. Create a new one for each attempt.
- With `confirm: true` the session is finalised at once and expires after 15 minutes. Use it only when you already have every customer field.
- `customer: { email }` attaches the session to an existing customer with that email. `feature_flags.always_create_new_customer: true` forces a new one; leave it off.
- `product_collection_id` sells a product collection; pass `product_cart: []` with it ([products.md](products.md)).
- Mandate-only subscriptions for on-demand charging use `subscription_data.on_demand` ([subscriptions.md](subscriptions.md)).

## Response and return URL

`checkoutSessions.create` returns `session_id` and `checkout_url`. `checkout_url` is null when the session is created with `confirm: true`; then `client_secret`, `publishable_key` and `payment_id` are set for the inline flow. `publishable_key` is a per-session value, not an API key.

After payment the customer lands on `return_url` with query parameters:

```text
https://example.com/checkout/success?payment_id=pay_xxx&status=succeeded&email=customer%40example.com
https://example.com/checkout/success?subscription_id=sub_xxx&status=active&license_key=LK-001
```

- `payment_id` (one-time) or `subscription_id` (subscription). There is no `session_id` parameter.
- `status`: `succeeded` or `active` on success, `failed`, `expired`, or `processing` and `requires_*` while it settles.
- `license_key` (comma-separated) and `email` when available.

Show a "thanks, we are confirming your payment" page and wait for the webhook. Treat a missing or `processing` status as unknown.

## Overlay and inline checkout

The `dodopayments-checkout` browser package opens the checkout session URL in a modal (`overlay`) or in an element on your page (`inline`). The server route above still creates the session; the browser never sees an API key.

```bash
npm install dodopayments-checkout
```

```typescript
import { DodoPayments } from 'dodopayments-checkout';

// Call once when the app loads, not before each checkout.
DodoPayments.Initialize({
  mode: 'test', // 'live' in production
  displayType: 'overlay', // or 'inline'
  onEvent: (event) => console.log('Checkout event:', event),
});

export async function openCheckout(planId: 'starter' | 'pro') {
  const response = await fetch('/api/checkout', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ planId }),
  });
  const { checkoutUrl } = (await response.json()) as { checkoutUrl: string };
  DodoPayments.Checkout.open({ checkoutUrl }); // inline: also pass elementId: 'dodo-inline-checkout'
}
```

For inline mode, render `<div id="dodo-inline-checkout"></div>` where the form should appear.

## Static payment links

For no-code sharing, link straight to a product. No API call is involved, and access still comes from the webhook.

```text
https://checkout.dodopayments.com/buy/pdt_example?quantity=1&email=customer@example.com&redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2Fsuccess
```

Test-mode products live on `https://test.checkout.dodopayments.com/buy/{product_id}`. Other query parameters: `fullName`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `country`, `city`, `state`, `zipCode`, `addressLine`, `paymentCurrency`, and `metadata_<key>`.

## Retrieve and preview

```typescript
const status = await client.checkoutSessions.retrieve('cks_session_id');
console.log(status.payment_status, status.payment_id);

const preview = await client.checkoutSessions.preview({
  product_cart: [{ product_id: 'pdt_pro_monthly', quantity: 1 }],
  billing_currency: 'EUR',
});
console.log(preview.current_breakup.total_amount);
```

## Common mistakes

- Granting access from `return_url` query parameters. Wait for the verified webhook.
- Accepting a `pdt_` ID or a price from the browser. Map a plan slug to an allowlisted product ID on the server and reject non-positive quantities.
- Calling the SDK from browser code. The key is secret.
- Forgetting `environment: 'test_mode'` in development; the default is live mode.
- Amounts in major units. USD 10.00 is `1000`.
- Reusing a `checkout_url`. Create a new checkout session per attempt.

# Customers

## Contents

- [Link app users to customers](#link-app-users-to-customers)
