## Product model

- Each product has one `price` object whose `type` is `one_time_price`, `recurring_price` or `usage_based_price`. The type cannot change after creation; create a new product instead.
- `tax_category` is required: `digital_products`, `saas`, `e_book` or `edtech`.
- Amounts are in the smallest currency unit.
- There is no delete. Archive products you no longer sell.
- Products are per mode. A test-mode `pdt_` ID does not exist in live mode.

## One-time product

```typescript
const product = await client.products.create({
  name: 'Pro Bundle',
  tax_category: 'digital_products',
  price: {
    type: 'one_time_price',
    currency: 'USD',
    price: 9900, // USD 99.00
    discount: 0,
    purchasing_power_parity: false,
  },
});
console.log(product.product_id);
```

## Subscription product

```typescript
const plan = await client.products.create({
  name: 'Pro Monthly',
  tax_category: 'saas',
  price: {
    type: 'recurring_price',
    currency: 'USD',
    price: 2900, // USD 29.00 per month
    discount: 0,
    payment_frequency_count: 1,
    payment_frequency_interval: 'Month',
    subscription_period_count: 1,
    subscription_period_interval: 'Month',
    purchasing_power_parity: false,
  },
});
```

## Usage-based product

Create the meter first ([usage-billing.md](usage-billing.md)), then attach it:

```typescript
const metered = await client.products.create({
  name: 'API Calls',
  tax_category: 'saas',
  price: {
    type: 'usage_based_price',
    currency: 'USD',
    discount: 0,
    fixed_price: 0, // optional base fee per cycle
    payment_frequency_count: 1,
    payment_frequency_interval: 'Month',
    subscription_period_count: 1,
    subscription_period_interval: 'Month',
    purchasing_power_parity: false,
    meters: [{ meter_id: 'mtr_api_calls', price_per_unit: '0.01', free_threshold: 1000 }],
  },
});
```

`price_per_unit` is a decimal string in the smallest currency unit.

## Update, archive, list

```typescript
await client.products.update('pdt_pro_bundle', {
  name: 'Pro Bundle',
  description: 'Includes all pro features',
  metadata: { tier: 'premium' },
});

await client.products.archive('pdt_pro_bundle');
await client.products.unarchive('pdt_pro_bundle');

for await (const item of client.products.list()) {
  console.log(item.product_id, item.name);
}
```

`update` also accepts `price`, `tax_category`, `pricing_mode` and `entitlements`. A price change applies to new customers only; move existing subscribers with `client.subscriptions.changePlan` ([subscriptions.md](subscriptions.md)).

## Images

The upload URL is valid for 60 seconds, so upload right away:

```typescript
import fs from 'node:fs';

const upload = await client.products.images.update('pdt_pro_bundle', { force_update: true });
const response = await fetch(upload.url, {
  method: 'PUT',
  body: fs.readFileSync('./product.png'),
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'image/png' },
});
if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Image upload failed');
```

## Add-ons

```typescript
const addon = await client.addons.create({
  name: 'Extra seat',
  tax_category: 'saas',
  currency: 'USD',
  price: 900,
});
```

Sell an add-on through `product_cart[].addons` on the checkout session ([checkout.md](checkout.md)).

## Product collections

A collection groups products for one checkout (and for plan switching in the customer portal).

```typescript
const collection = await client.productCollections.create({
  name: 'Plans',
  groups: [{ group_name: 'Monthly', products: [{ product_id: 'pdt_starter' }, { product_id: 'pdt_pro' }] }],
});

const session = await client.checkoutSessions.create({
  product_collection_id: collection.id,
  product_cart: [], // required and empty for collection checkout
  return_url: 'https://example.com/return',
});
```

## Digital file delivery

Files are delivered through a `digital_files` entitlement attached to the product. Dodo creates the grant on purchase.

```typescript
// openAsBlob needs Node.js 20+
import { openAsBlob } from 'node:fs';

const entitlement = await client.entitlements.create({
  name: 'Pro Bundle Files',
  integration_type: 'digital_files',
  integration_config: { digital_file_ids: [] },
});

const form = new FormData();
form.append('filename', 'pro-bundle.zip'); // append filename before file
form.append('file', await openAsBlob('./pro-bundle.zip'), 'pro-bundle.zip');
await client.entitlements.files.upload(entitlement.id, { body: form });

// `entitlements` replaces every entitlement on the product: send the full list.
await client.products.update('pdt_pro_bundle', { entitlements: [{ entitlement_id: entitlement.id }] });

const grants = await client.customers.listEntitlementGrants('cus_abc123');
const downloadUrl = grants.items[0]?.digital_product_delivery?.files[0]?.download_url; // expires in about 15 minutes
```

## Short links

```typescript
const shortLink = await client.products.shortLinks.create('pdt_pro_bundle', { slug: 'pro-bundle' });
console.log(shortLink.short_url);
```

## Common mistakes

- Looking for a delete endpoint, or trying to switch a product between one-time, subscription and usage-based pricing.
- Expecting a price edit to reprice existing subscribers.
- Omitting `tax_category`.
- Hardcoding prices in the client. Read the product on the server.
- A non-empty `product_cart` with `product_collection_id`.

# Refunds and disputes

## Contents

- [Issue a refund](#issue-a-refund)
- [Refund statuses and webhooks](#refund-statuses-and-webhooks)
- [Disputes](#disputes)
- [Dispute webhooks](#dispute-webhooks)
- [Common mistakes](#common-mistakes)

Dodo, as Merchant of Record, moves the money and runs the card-network dispute process. Your app decides who keeps access. A refund is a live-mode write: confirm the payment ID and amount with the user first.

## Issue a refund

```typescript
// Full refund
const refund = await client.refunds.create({ payment_id: 'pay_abc123' });
console.log(refund.refund_id, refund.status);

// Partial refund by line item. Omit amount to refund the whole item.
const partial = await client.refunds.create({
  payment_id: 'pay_abc123',
  items: [{ item_id: 'item_1' }, { item_id: 'item_2', amount: 2500 }],
});
```

Read the refundable items first with `client.payments.retrieveLineItems('pay_abc123')`. If a refund call errors or times out, list the payment's refunds before retrying, so the customer is not refunded twice.

## Refund statuses and webhooks

| `status` | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pending` | Processing; the money has not left yet |
| `succeeded` | Returned to the customer |
| `review` | Under review; do not assume success |
| `failed` | Not refunded |

Act on the verified webhook ([webhooks.md](webhooks.md)):

```typescript
import DodoPayments from 'dodopayments';

export async function handleRefundWebhook(event: DodoPayments.UnwrapWebhookEvent) {
  if (event.type === 'refund.succeeded') {
    const refund = event.data;
    if (!refund.is_partial) {
      await revokeCustomerAccess(refund.customer.customer_id);
    } else {
      // Remove access only for items with nothing left to refund.
      const { items } = await client.payments.retrieveLineItems(refund.payment_id);
      const fullyRefunded = items.filter((item) => item.refundable_amount === 0).map((item) => item.items_id);
      await revokeItemAccess(refund.customer.customer_id, fullyRefunded);
    }
  }
  if (event.type === 'refund.failed') {
    await alertSupport(event.data.refund_id, event.data.reason); // keep access
  }
}
```

License keys from a refunded one-time payment are disabled by Dodo; see [license-keys.md](license-keys.md).

## Disputes

Customers open disputes through their card network. You can only read them, and you submit evidence in the dashboard (there is no evidence API) within 10 days of the dispute opening.

```typescript
const dispute = await client.disputes.retrieve('dis_abc123');
console.log(dispute.dispute_status, dispute.amount, dispute.customer.customer_id);

for await (const item of client.disputes.list()) {
  console.log(item.dispute_id, item.dispute_status);
}
```

## Dispute webhooks

| Webhook | Access |
|---|---|
| `dispute.opened` | Revoke while open; gather evidence |
| `dispute.challenged` | Keep revoked; evidence under review |
| `dispute.won` | Restore |
| `dispute.cancelled` | Restore; the customer withdrew it |
| `dispute.accepted`, `dispute.lost`, `dispute.expired` | Keep revoked |

Dispute webhook payloads have no customer field. Read the dispute to find the customer:

```typescript
async function customerForDispute(disputeId: string) {
  const dispute = await client.disputes.retrieve(disputeId);
  return dispute.customer.customer_id;
}

export async function handleDisputeWebhook(event: DodoPayments.UnwrapWebhookEvent) {
  if (event.type === 'dispute.opened') {
    await revokeCustomerAccess(await customerForDispute(event.data.dispute_id));
  }
  if (event.type === 'dispute.won' || event.type === 'dispute.cancelled') {
    await restoreCustomerAccess(await customerForDispute(event.data.dispute_id));
  }
}
```

## Common mistakes

- Refunding without deciding on access. Revoke access for a full refund of a non-refundable product.
- Revoking access to every item on a partial refund.
- Restoring access on `dispute.accepted`, `dispute.lost` or `dispute.expired`.
- Reading `customer` from a dispute webhook payload; it is not there.
- Retrying a failed refund call without checking existing refunds first.

